 of retail space and 743 residential units. Empire State Realty Trust, Inc. was established on July 29, 2011, and was incorporated in 2011 in Maryland and is based in New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony E. Malkin | Chairman & CEO | Age 63 | Compensation: $3.2M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 642 people. Revenue per employee of $1.2M ranks in the below the sector median among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $79K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $39K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Empire State Realty Trust, Inc. is a small-cap real estate business with a $1.5B market cap on $768M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $51M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 5.74\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.1% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 8.4% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 39% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other 